{cot}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139539078 17592186576411 false] [17592186332687 1074 "We multiply out the parentheses and then use the identities $$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},\n$$ and $$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},\n$$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539078 17592186576411 true] [17592186332687 1074 "We multiply out the parentheses and then use the identities $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},$ and $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539078 17592186576411 false] [17592186332688 1071 "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" 13194139539078 17592186576411 true] [17592186332688 1071 "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139539078 17592186576411 false] [17592186332688 1074 "We use the identity $$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},\n$$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539078 17592186576411 true] [17592186332688 1074 "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539078 17592186576411 false] [17592186332689 1071 "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" 13194139539078 17592186576411 true] [17592186332689 1071 "$\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139539078 17592186576411 false] [17592186332690 1071 "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" 13194139539078 17592186576411 true] [17592186332690 1071 "$\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139539078 17592186576411 false] [17592186332691 1071 "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" 13194139539078 17592186576411 true] [17592186332691 1071 "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139539078 17592186576411 false] [17592186332691 1074 "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡4x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{tan}⁡4x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\n$$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the identity $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=4x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539078 17592186576411 true] [17592186332691 1074 "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡4x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the identity $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=4x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539078 17592186576411 false] [17592186332692 1071 "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" 13194139539078 17592186576411 true] [17592186332692 1071 "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139539078 17592186576411 false] [17592186332693 1071 "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" 13194139539078 1759